Oz: the player's own predicted events play once, whatever the server numbers them. id's cgame numbered
the server's events and the predicted ones in one sequence and played any slot whose event changed, so
where the server's game had an event the prediction didn't (A51's: a footstep as a running jump lands
and takes off again), or one a step earlier or later, every event after it moved a slot and played
again: jumps and shots heard twice on community servers whose game moves the player a little
differently. Each predicted event is kept with the command time it ran at (CG_PredictPlayerState): one
of the server's plays only if no predicted event of its kind and parm from about then played, and one
the prediction runs again plays only if it didn't run at about that time before. cg_ozEventOnce 0 is
id's way, for comparing; cg_showmiss 1 prints "event <n> (seq <n>) played already".

